      "side": 1,
      "message": "What\u0027s the advantage of matching these conventions? There has to be a reason to doing it this way other than \"they did it this way\". Let\u0027s put some reasoning as to why these conventions are good and why are we following them here.\n\nThere\u0027s people patching dbus-sensors downstream for a single-binary design to reduce the compressed rofs size.\n\nAlso you can have a recipe level selection of hardware support via meson options. Separate binaries are not required for that.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 350,
        "endChar": 27
      },
      "revId": "c44aca752c6b83ea684073d19836ea36d546b321",
