        "id": 1002134
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-01T13:56:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When I picked per-type binaries, part of it was matching existing convention, but I also expected each type would need its own D-Bus interface, with its own property names, transition enum and state enum, so the type-specific behavior around that would live in its own binary.\n\nThat\u0027s not the case anymore with `State.Device`: every type binds to the same property set and enums, so what\u0027s left type-specific is configuration, not logic — the daemon just finds the actual devices from entity-manager at runtime. Splitting that into one process per type at that point wouldn\u0027t be separating any logic, just processes.\n\nI\u0027ve moved the design to a single type-agnostic daemon and written this out in the Alternatives section.",
      "parentUuid": "9a59d8a3_c6c53384",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 348,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 350,
        "endChar": 27
